# The SC2 editor owns the bytes of everything under the map. Git must not guess
# at line endings on top of that: the editor rewrites every file it saves to
# CRLF, and a checkout that converts them again turns one changed field into a
# whole-file diff, which is what made every pull a conflict.
#
# -text means "store and check out these bytes exactly", so the only diffs left
# are the ones somebody actually made.
LobotomyShiphold.SC2Map/** -text
